{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "type": "docs.detail",
  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "name": "getting-started",
    "description": "Add the design system to your project and start building.",
    "category": "guide",
    "keywords": [
      "quick start",
      "setup",
      "install"
    ],
    "title": "Getting Started",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "quick-start-with-ai",
        "title": "Quick Start with AI",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Paste this into your AI coding tool and let it handle the setup:"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "text",
            "code": "Install @astryxdesign/core, @stylexjs/stylex, @astryxdesign/theme-neutral, and @astryxdesign/cli in this project, then run `astryx init` to set up agent docs. Read the generated files to learn the conventions.",
            "label": "Set up the design system"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Then give it a look. Every app gets a theme whether or not anyone picks one, so it is worth one question at setup rather than revisiting screens later that were built around the wrong look:"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "text",
            "code": "Ask me what look and feel this app should have. Run `astryx theme list`, install the closest theme package, and run `theme add <slug>`; use `--package` when owners share a slug. Import `themes` and `defaultThemeSlug` from the generated module once and pass `themes[defaultThemeSlug]` to `<Theme>`. Customize with `defineTheme({extends: importedTheme, ...})`. Use `theme eject` only when I ask for an independent source fork. Default to neutral if I have no preference, and show me the result before moving on.",
            "label": "Give it a look"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "install",
        "title": "Install",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Astryx requires React 19 or later: `react` and `react-dom` >= 19.0.0 are peer dependencies of `@astryxdesign/core`."
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Add the core package and its `@stylexjs/stylex` peer dependency, plus a theme and the CLI."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "npm install @astryxdesign/core @stylexjs/stylex @astryxdesign/theme-neutral @astryxdesign/cli",
            "label": "Terminal"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Then run `astryx init` to install the AI agent cheat sheet (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md). It's non-interactive; no prompts; so it's safe for AI agents, CI, and scripts. Add `--all` for pointers to the theme and page-building workflows."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "astryx init",
            "label": "Terminal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "upgrade",
        "title": "Upgrade",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Upgrade every Astryx package your app lists in one command, to the same release. Each theme names the exact Core release it works with, so a theme left on an older release no longer matches the new Core."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "npm install @astryxdesign/core@latest @astryxdesign/theme-neutral@latest @astryxdesign/cli@latest\nastryx upgrade --from <old Core version> --apply",
            "label": "Terminal"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Add every other Astryx package your app lists to the same command, and pass the Core version you had before to `--from`. If your package manager holds new releases back, exempt the whole `@astryxdesign/*` scope; in pnpm, `minimumReleaseAgeExclude: ['@astryxdesign/*']`. Exempting only some of its packages installs packages from different releases side by side."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "install-once",
        "title": "Install once, use everywhere",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Install the CLI once for your computer too, and the astryx command works in any folder, for you and for any coding agent, even before a project exists. Inside a project, the project's own version still answers, so a global install never changes what your team and CI get. Keep it in the project as well; that is the recommended setup."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "npm install -g @astryxdesign/cli",
            "label": "Terminal"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Project, global, or both: `astryx docs global/project-global-or-both`. Everything else about global mode: `astryx docs global`."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "add-base-css-and-a-theme",
        "title": "Add base CSS and a theme",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Import the reset and base styles in your global CSS. Then run `astryx theme add neutral`; the generated app module imports the theme’s production CSS and font CSS."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "css",
            "code": "@import '@astryxdesign/core/reset.css';\n@import '@astryxdesign/core/astryx.css';",
            "label": "globals.css"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Run `astryx theme list` to see every theme."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "tsx",
            "code": "import {Theme} from '@astryxdesign/core/theme';\nimport {themes, defaultThemeSlug} from './astryx-themes';\n\n<Theme theme={themes[defaultThemeSlug]}><App /></Theme>",
            "label": "App root"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "style": "unordered",
            "items": [
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-neutral`: muted and minimal; a good starting point",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-butter`: warm, golden tones with blue accents",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-chocolate`: rich chocolate and caramel tones",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-gothic`: dark-only theme with ink and noir influences",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-matcha`: earthy greens and botanical tones",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-stone`: warm neutrals inspired by sandstone",
              "`@astryxdesign/theme-y2k`: playful early-2000s pop aesthetic"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "These stylesheets are cascade-layered: the reset loads in @layer reset and component styles in @layer astryx-base. If your project has existing global CSS, a legacy reset, or Tailwind, declare the layer order explicitly and assign every stylesheet to a layer deliberately: unlayered styles and later layers both override astryx-base regardless of specificity. Before building screens, read the two cascade layer sections of `astryx docs migration/migration-setup`."
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Run `astryx docs use-a-theme` for the full theming guide."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "add-your-first-component",
        "title": "Add your first component",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Import each component from its own entry, the path `astryx component <Name>` prints. This keeps bundles small and makes intent clear."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "tsx",
            "code": "import {Button} from '@astryxdesign/core/Button';\nimport {VStack} from '@astryxdesign/core/VStack';\n\nexport default function Page() {\n  return (\n    <VStack gap={2}>\n      <Button label=\"Hello Astryx\" onClick={() => alert('Hi!')} />\n    </VStack>\n  );\n}",
            "label": "app/page.tsx"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "customize-with-stylex",
        "title": "Customize with StyleX",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Astryx components support various styling solutions, from plain CSS and `className` to Tailwind and CSS-in-JS. See `astryx docs styling` for the full guide. Astryx also has a deep integration with [StyleX](https://stylexjs.com/), an atomic CSS-in-JS library: create styles with `stylex.create()` and pass them to components with the `xstyle` prop."
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "tsx",
            "code": "import * as stylex from '@stylexjs/stylex';\n\nconst overrides = stylex.create({\n  save: { alignSelf: 'flex-end', marginTop: 16 },\n});\n\n<Button label=\"Save\" xstyle={overrides.save} />",
            "label": "Style overrides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "example-apps",
        "title": "Example Apps",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "For a full working project, clone one of the example apps from the repo. These are complete setups with routing, theming, and components wired together."
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "headers": [
              "Example",
              "Stack",
              "Path"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Next.js",
                "Next.js + theme CSS",
                "[apps/example-nextjs](https://github.com/meta/astryx/tree/main/apps/example-nextjs)"
              ],
              [
                "Next.js + StyleX",
                "Next.js + StyleX for custom styles",
                "[apps/example-nextjs-stylex](https://github.com/meta/astryx/tree/main/apps/example-nextjs-stylex)"
              ],
              [
                "Next.js + Tailwind",
                "Next.js + Tailwind bridge",
                "[apps/example-nextjs-tailwind](https://github.com/meta/astryx/tree/main/apps/example-nextjs-tailwind)"
              ],
              [
                "Vite + Tailwind",
                "Vite + Tailwind bridge",
                "[apps/example-vite-tailwind](https://github.com/meta/astryx/tree/main/apps/example-vite-tailwind)"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "git clone https://github.com/meta/astryx.git\ncd astryx/apps/example-nextjs\nnpm install\nnpm run dev",
            "label": "Clone and run an example"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "explore-the-cli",
        "title": "Explore the CLI",
        "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "The CLI is your reference for components, tokens, templates, and docs. For reliable invocation (especially with AI assistants), add this script to your package.json:"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "json",
            "code": "\"scripts\": {\n  \"astryx\": \"node node_modules/@astryxdesign/cli/clients/cli/bin/astryx.mjs\"\n}",
            "label": "package.json"
          },
          {
            "type": "prose",
            "text": "Then discover what's available:"
          },
          {
            "type": "code",
            "lang": "bash",
            "code": "astryx component          # list all components\nastryx component Button   # props, usage, theming for Button\nastryx docs               # list all doc topics\nastryx template --list    # available page templates\nastryx docs tokens        # spacing, color, radius reference",
            "label": "Terminal"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "links": {
      "up": "astryx docs guides",
      "previous": "astryx docs browser-support",
      "next": "astryx docs is-my-code-good"
    }
  },
